    "narrative": "For LawDog today, we are prioritizing high-upside speed and matchup stability. **Daulton Varsho** (64.82) and **Lawrence Butler** (64.30) represent our strongest plays, as both benefit from significant platoon advantages against right-handed opposition that push them toward the top of our daily efficiency rankings. **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.13) also stands out; while his raw power is modest, his spot in the #2 hole against a vulnerable arm like Liberatore makes him a primary engine for our Runs category today. **Bryson Stott** (60.17) rounds out our core starts, as his matchup against Palmquist provides a rare confluence of a high-xERA starter and favorable delivery mechanics that keep our stolen base probability high, countering the drag of a same-handed platoon disadvantage.\n\nWe have a tight margin at the bottom of our lineup, with **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.36) and **Jonathan Aranda** (43.48) occupying the final spots. **Masyn Winn** (38.90) serves as our most notable bench decision; despite his utility, he falls below our 40.0 floor due to a tough matchup against Bratt and a negative park factor, forcing us to prioritize the platoon ceiling of our active starters instead. We remain cautious regarding **Cal Raleigh** (49.29) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (49.02); both face pitchers with xERAs under 4.00, introducing enough risk to dampen their output. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Luis Arraez** remain sidelined or unavailable, the roster remains deep enough to maintain efficiency without overextending our games-played budget. We are monitoring all lineups closely for late changes, as the lack of an elite ceiling for the bottom third of our order leaves little room for error if weather or late scratches disrupt the current slate.",
